---
description: Standards for course roadmap and README authoring
globs: ["README.md", "COURSE_MODULES.md", "[0-9][0-9] - */README.md"]
alwaysApply: false
---

You are editing a course README, a module README, or the course roadmap.

When a command is active, follow its declared reads; do not load the ad-hoc
path below or a different command's manifest.

- `/write-module-readme` — expand within those reads and [[Canonical sources]]
  in `docs/standards/readme-authoring.md` when a scoped read does not
  establish an answer.
- `/review-module` — follow [[Module-review manifest]], applicable
  [[Conditional reads]], and [[Module-review bar]] in
  `docs/standards/notebook-authoring-checklist.md`.

For ad-hoc edits with no active command:

- **`COURSE_MODULES.md`** — roadmap ownership only. Do not add notebook
  sequences, exercises, or code.
- **Root `README.md`** — edit in place. Its own existing structure is the
  only structural source for that file; do not load readme-authoring.
- **Numbered module `README.md`** — read
  `docs/standards/readme-authoring.md` and the [[Canonical sources]] it
  names, then apply [[Required structure]] and the
  [[Design-complete definition]]. For folder or notebook naming, read
  [[Module folders]] and [[Notebook files]] in
  `docs/standards/naming-conventions.md`. When editing
  [[readme-authoring#Learning objectives|Learning objectives]], also read
  [[Audience assumptions]] and [[Production framing]] in
  `docs/standards/teaching-guidelines.md`.

For new module design, the author should use `/write-module-readme` (not
ad-hoc chat) so reads and stop conditions load consistently.

For a numbered module `README.md`, readme-authoring and the matching
`COURSE_MODULES.md` row are canonical. If the README conflicts with them,
follow those sources.

Automatic-write restrictions are owned by the [[Author-only writes]] section
in `AGENTS.md`.
